/*
This file documents the drop-in adapter for PaddleOCR's official Android SDK.
It is intentionally .disabled so HanScan V3 builds immediately with bundled ML Kit OCR.

Official API (PaddleOCR Android deployment docs):

PaddleOCR ocr = PaddleOCR.create(
    context,
    new PaddleOCRConfig(...),
    new EngineConfig(4),
    "models/det/inference.onnx",
    "models/rec/inference.onnx",
    "models/rec/inference.yml"
);
OCRRunResult result = ocr.recognize(imageBytes);

To enable:
1. Copy official PaddleOCR deploy/ppocr-android/ppocr-sdk into project root.
2. include(":ppocr-sdk") in settings.gradle.kts.
3. implementation(project(":ppocr-sdk")) in app/build.gradle.kts.
4. Put PP-OCRv5_mobile or PP-OCRv6 ONNX models under ppocr-sdk/src/main/assets/models/.
5. Implement the same output conversion used by MlKitChineseOcrEngine -> OcrResult/OcrChar.
*/
